 deficits associated with parkinsonism</article-title><source>Neurol Clin</source><year>1992</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>451</fpage><lpage>469</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1584184</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mandir</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lenz</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Gildenberg PL, Tasker RR</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical Pathophysiology in Parkinson's Disease</article-title><source>Textbook of Stereotactic and Functional Neurosurgery</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>New York , McGraw-Hill</publisher-name><fpage>1133</fpage><lpage>1137</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>